WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.165 --> 00:00:02.314
- So Chrissy Teigen just happened to be

00:00:02.314 --> 00:00:03.980
at BuzzFeed as I was writing this post,

00:00:03.980 --> 00:00:05.669
and I told her, "Your egg's didn't win,"

00:00:05.669 --> 00:00:09.368
and she said, "God damn it,"
and she just walked away.

00:00:09.368 --> 00:00:11.368
(music)

00:00:12.774 --> 00:00:14.512
Today I'm gonna be making five famous

00:00:14.512 --> 00:00:15.908
scrambled egg recipes to find out

00:00:15.908 --> 00:00:17.486
which one is actually the best.

00:00:17.486 --> 00:00:19.374
I set up five recipes to replicate

00:00:19.374 --> 00:00:21.262
exactly how the celebrities do it.

00:00:21.262 --> 00:00:22.662
We have Gordon Ramsay,

00:00:22.662 --> 00:00:23.495
Martha Stewart,

00:00:23.495 --> 00:00:24.471
Heston Blumenthal,

00:00:24.471 --> 00:00:25.368
Anthony Bourdain,

00:00:25.368 --> 00:00:27.709
and then for a wild card,
I have Chrissy Teigen.

00:00:27.709 --> 00:00:29.161
I lined up all the
ingredients on the recipes.

00:00:29.161 --> 00:00:30.751
I measured them precisely,

00:00:30.751 --> 00:00:32.556
and I got toast ready for all of them,

00:00:32.556 --> 00:00:33.706
so we can all try it.

00:00:33.706 --> 00:00:36.044
So the whole playing
field's completely level.

00:00:36.044 --> 00:00:38.048
Three of my friends
are gonna come down and

00:00:38.048 --> 00:00:40.631
taste them with me to see
which one is actually the best.

00:00:40.631 --> 00:00:42.656
So let's get this scrambled
egg showdown crackin'.

00:00:42.656 --> 00:00:43.489
(chicken squawks)

00:00:43.489 --> 00:00:44.485
Anthony Bourdain's eggs.

00:00:44.485 --> 00:00:45.916
He whips them just until

00:00:45.916 --> 00:00:48.948
there's a ripple of white
and yellow, not all the way.

00:00:48.948 --> 00:00:53.046
And then he cooks them
in a hot pan with butter.

00:00:53.046 --> 00:00:54.909
And he cooks them in a figure eight motion

00:00:54.909 --> 00:00:58.315
until they're cooked, and
this one cooks really fast.

00:00:58.315 --> 00:01:00.315
(music)

00:01:03.860 --> 00:01:06.409
Martha Stewart follows
a pretty traditional way

00:01:06.409 --> 00:01:07.647
to scramble her eggs.

00:01:07.647 --> 00:01:09.109
She thinks that if you have good eggs,

00:01:09.109 --> 00:01:10.601
you don't need to add anything to them.

00:01:10.601 --> 00:01:13.420
So she cooks them in a pan
with butter on low heat.

00:01:13.420 --> 00:01:15.292
Very traditional, and she pushes them all

00:01:15.292 --> 00:01:18.067
towards the center in this ripple motion

00:01:18.067 --> 00:01:20.090
to create kind of these ribbons,

00:01:20.090 --> 00:01:21.753
that are like really beautiful.

00:01:21.753 --> 00:01:23.532
And then she seasons with salt and pepper

00:01:23.532 --> 00:01:26.145
right at the end, and that's it.

00:01:26.145 --> 00:01:29.142
(upbeat music)

00:01:29.142 --> 00:01:32.255
Gordon Ramsay's internet famous eggs,

00:01:32.255 --> 00:01:36.086
cooks them in a pot, he serves
them with chunks of butter

00:01:36.086 --> 00:01:40.538
and he puts them on a low
burner for 30 seconds,

00:01:40.538 --> 00:01:42.596
he takes them off,

00:01:42.596 --> 00:01:44.655
stirs them for 20 more seconds,

00:01:44.655 --> 00:01:46.375
then puts them on for 30 seconds,

00:01:46.375 --> 00:01:48.173
puts them on again for
the last 20 seconds,

00:01:48.173 --> 00:01:49.463
and throws some creme fresh in

00:01:49.463 --> 00:01:52.284
to cool them down really
quickly, and that's it.

00:01:52.284 --> 00:01:53.832
(music)

00:01:53.832 --> 00:01:55.771
Chrissy Teigan's scrambled eggs are

00:01:55.771 --> 00:01:57.660
I'm guessing, obviously gonna be good

00:01:57.660 --> 00:02:00.892
because she puts a whole
quarter cup of cream in them.

00:02:00.892 --> 00:02:04.097
And she cooks them with
three tablespoons of butter,

00:02:04.097 --> 00:02:05.851
so it's just fat on fat.

00:02:05.851 --> 00:02:07.517
She cooks them on super low heat

00:02:07.517 --> 00:02:09.397
and this takes about 20 minutes,

00:02:09.397 --> 00:02:11.040
it's so low heat, actually.

00:02:11.040 --> 00:02:12.422
She seasons the egg mixture itself

00:02:12.422 --> 00:02:14.012
so I think these ones,

00:02:14.012 --> 00:02:15.521
they're gonna taste like butter and cream

00:02:15.521 --> 00:02:18.058
so they're gonna be pretty freakin' good.

00:02:18.058 --> 00:02:20.058
(music)

00:02:25.133 --> 00:02:27.472
Heston Blumenthal has
a very strange method,

00:02:27.472 --> 00:02:30.266
when he combines milk,
cream, eggs, salt and pepper

00:02:30.266 --> 00:02:32.900
in a double boiler with a whisk.

00:02:32.900 --> 00:02:34.846
And he puts them over
gently simmering water

00:02:34.846 --> 00:02:36.246
and stirs them with a rubber spatula

00:02:36.246 --> 00:02:38.138
until they're just barely cooked.

00:02:38.138 --> 00:02:40.664
The gentle heat is supposed to keep them

00:02:40.664 --> 00:02:42.131
pretty soft and moist.

00:02:42.131 --> 00:02:44.324
And I'm so sorry for using the word moist.

00:02:44.324 --> 00:02:46.324
(music)

00:02:47.963 --> 00:02:49.808
- It's whatever, it's
literally whatever eggs.

00:02:49.808 --> 00:02:51.191
- It's very flat.

00:02:51.191 --> 00:02:52.024
- Yeah.

00:02:52.024 --> 00:02:54.813
- It looks like it was
on the bottom of the pan

00:02:54.813 --> 00:02:55.899
and they like just scraped it off.

00:02:55.899 --> 00:02:57.637
- They didn't mix it well,
look at all the colors.

00:02:57.637 --> 00:03:00.072
- White, yellow, yellow

00:03:00.072 --> 00:03:02.232
- Yeah, it's like it's not very mixed.

00:03:02.232 --> 00:03:03.723
- They're standard, they're okay.

00:03:03.723 --> 00:03:06.063
- Who is it, Anthony Bourdain.

00:03:06.063 --> 00:03:07.507
- I can see how he got this texture,

00:03:07.507 --> 00:03:09.459
he has that figure eight technique,

00:03:09.459 --> 00:03:11.216
so it's not mixed very well.

00:03:11.216 --> 00:03:12.513
- Don't do the figure eight.

00:03:12.513 --> 00:03:13.691
- No, no figure eight.

00:03:13.691 --> 00:03:15.247
- These are a little richer.

00:03:15.247 --> 00:03:17.300
- The last one was like,
anybody making those eggs

00:03:17.300 --> 00:03:19.304
this one was like probably like
your friend, and he's like,

00:03:19.304 --> 00:03:21.249
"Ooh yeah, let me just put some
milk in it and whip it up."

00:03:21.249 --> 00:03:23.089
And you're like, "Oh cool, thanks."

00:03:23.089 --> 00:03:24.308
- Martha.

00:03:24.308 --> 00:03:25.597
- This is like how I make my eggs.

00:03:25.597 --> 00:03:27.896
- Elevated basic eggs, which
is like what Martha does best.

00:03:27.896 --> 00:03:30.051
- Did you just call Martha Stewart basic?

00:03:30.051 --> 00:03:30.985
